(364, 1846, 'Working', 140, -2, 'Optimized GBP Profile Content\nBusiness Name\n\nThe Fleece Inn, Dolphinholme\n\nBusiness Description (750 characters max)\n\nâ€œWinner of the Countryside Alliance Best Pub in the North of England 2025, The Fleece Inn is an award-winning country pub nestled in the heart of Dolphinholme on the edge of the Forest of Bowland. Enjoy exceptional seasonal fare crafted from locally-sourced ingredientsâ€”including Dewlay cheeses, Honeywells meats, and house honeyâ€”paired with Bowland Brewery ales at our charming oak-beamed pub. Relax in our nine elegantly appointed rooms or self-contained apartment. With a village shop, EV charging, and a warm community spirit, weâ€™re more than a pubâ€”weâ€™re at the heart of rural life.â€\n\nHighlights / Summary (for GBP bullets or featured attributes)\n\nAwarded Best Pub in the North of England â€“ Countryside Alliance 2025 \nfleeceinn.co.uk\nLancaster Guardian\n\nSeasonal menus using locally-sourced produce (within 10 miles) \nfleeceinn.co.uk\n\nCharming bar & dining rooms with open fires and antique details \nThe Guardian\nCAMRA - The Campaign for Real Ale\n\nOn-site village shop offering essentials and local products \nThe Guardian\nLancaster Guardian\n\nNine luxurious guest rooms + self-catering apartment \nfleeceinn.co.uk\nThe Guardian\n\nTwo 22 kW EV charging pointsâ€”supporting sustainable travel \nfleeceinn.co.uk\n\nForest of Bowland gatewayâ€”ideal for walking, cycling & countryside escapes \nfleeceinn.co.uk\nLancaster Guardian\n\nCommunity hubâ€”quiz nights, loyal locals, warm hospitality \nLancaster Guardian\nThe Guardian\n\nServices & Amenities (for GBP attributes)\n\nRestaurant / Pub Dining\n\nAccommodation: Rooms & Apartment\n\nVillage Shop\n\nEV Charging Stations\n\nSeasonal Menus\n\nOpen Fires / Rustic Ambience\n\nLocally-Sourced Produce\n\nEvent Hosting (e.g., quiz nights)\n\nPhoto Suggestions\n\nCozy interior shots: oak-beamed bar, roaring fireplaces\n\nSeasonal dishes, close-ups of kitchen specials\n\nExterior views surrounded by Forest of Bowland\n\nGuest rooms showcasing rustic-luxury details\n\nEV charging stations in use\n\nVillage shop and its display\n\nGroup shots from quiz nights or community events\n\nAdditional Recommendations for the Google Profile\n1. Encourage Reviews\n\nPrompt satisfied guests to leave reviews, particularly emphasizing: \"award-winning pub,\" \"luxury accommodation,\" \"village shop,\" and \"EV charging.\"\n\nHighlight reviews that mention community feel, comfort, local sourcing.\n\n2. Regular Posts & Updates\n\nShare posts about seasonal menu launches, special events (like quiz nights), awards, or countryside highlights.\n\nUse the â€œOfferâ€ or â€œEventâ€ post types for promotions or happenings.\n\n3. Use Q&A Strategically\n\nPreemptively add answers to FAQs such as:\n\nâ€œDo you have EV charging?â€ â†’ Yesâ€”two 22kW Type 2 chargers.\n\nâ€œIs there accommodation?â€ â†’ Nine rooms + self-contained apartment.\n\nâ€œDo you sell groceries or essentials?â€ â†’ Yes, our on-site village shop.\n\n4. Menu & Service Insights\n\nIf possible, upload a current menu or snapshots of the offeringsâ€”seasonal dishes, childrenâ€™s menu, wine/beer list.\n\nAdd â€œMenuâ€ to profile features if supported.\n\n5. Booking & Reservation Links\n\nEnsure booking options are integrated and visible.\n\nPromote room/apartment reservations and table bookings via Google if available.\n\n6. Local Content & Community Engagement\n\nUse GBP posts to mention local walks, nearby attractions, or Forest of Bowland highlights.\n\nPosition the pub as the perfect base for exploration, or point to Lancaster (7 miles away), Ribblehead, etc. \nfleeceinn.co.uk\nThe Guardian\n\n7. Performance & Analytics\n\nRegularly review GBP metricsâ€”search queries leading to the profile, customer actions (calls, bookings, direction requests).\n\nAdjust descriptions or add attributes based on insights (e.g., if \"EV charging\" is being searched often).\n\n8. SEO-Friendly Business Info\n\nUse keywords like \"award-winning country pub,\" \"rural pub with accommodation,\" \"Forest of Bowland pub & rooms,\" etc., subtly within profile text.\n\n9. Leverage Recognition\n\nOn milestone anniversaries or publicity moments (e.g., reaching final of national award), update your GBP â€œFrom the ownerâ€ or â€œAboutâ€ section to reflect and share that story.\n\nSummary Table\nSection	Optimised Content & Actions\nDescription	Highlight award, local produce, ambiance, accommodation, EV, and shop\nHighlights	Use bullet key win, sourcing, rooms, EV, community appeal\nPhotos	Showcase interiors, food, rooms, EV, shop, exterior\nReviews	Solicit focus on awards, community, comfort\nPosts & Q&A	Regular updates + anticipatory FAQs\nBooking Links	Ensure easy visibility for booking rooms and dining\nLocal focus	Emphasise countryside location, walking/cycling access, Lancaster proximity\nAnalytics	Monitor customer interactions, refine profile accordingly', '2025-08-25', '01:30:00', 1, ''),
