(2333, 1774, 'Working', 155, -2, 'Hi Caroline, Iâ€™m pleased to inform you that we have made the necessary changes in Salesforce, and all leads have now been successfully imported into 8 Eaton Lane. We will continue to monitor the leads closely to ensure that no additional leads are missed due to issues with other fields. If we identify any further problems, we will notify you and advise when logins would be required. Thank you for your patience and understanding. Regards Syed', '2025-09-01', '02:00:00', 0, NULL),
(2334, 1774, 'Working', 155, -2, 'â€‹Hi Caroline,\n\nThe issue still exists and will require liaising with Alicorn to get it resolved, as not all leads will reach Salesforce correctly until this is rectified.\nWhat Michael mentioned below is correct for 95% of the leads, but for the remaining 5% to work correctly, we still need to find a solution.\nIf youâ€™d like to have a quick call to share the 2FA, that works for me â€“ we can try to fix it before Alicorn takes a look. The only thing holding us back at the moment is the 2FA.\nI have already mentioned in another thread the leads that did not reach Salesforce during the bulk import. I am sharing them again here for your reference.\n\nLeads Not Imported:\np.khela@sky.com\n\ngiostylianou@gmail.com\n\naliieva.niiara@gmail.com\n\nsoner.cesur@ficommerce.com\n\n23tigerbergstrasse@gmail.com\n\nfz@fzukcontent.com\n\nyogivedd24@gmail.com\n\ndione.harrison24@icloud.com\n\nnikolausmm@gmail.com\n\nsophiademir134@gmail.com\n\nmary.toker@gmail.com\n\nfz.lemssouguer@gmail.com\n\nhrtt@hotmail.co.uk\n\nhexagonalcloudpattern@gmail.com\n\nnadayahyabader@gmail.com\n\nmb@bird.in\n\nravikumar_s@me.com\n\ninfo@midasantiquities.com\n\nhinaser@gmail.com\n\nbursars.climb.3y@icloud.com\n\nrobertmcphillips976@gmail.com\n\ns.parekh@kentons.co.uk\n\nrmasih90@yahoo.com\n\nteresa@tanco.uk\n\nasitaksischool@icloud.com\n\nkmalsayer@alsayergroup.com\n\nbradley@realuxinternational.com\n\nRasa.bagdonaviciute@ddre.global\n\nWe have records of all these leads in the website backend.\nHowever, we are unable to re-import them into Salesforce until the issues we have previously outlined are fully rectified.\n\n\nRegards\nSyed â€‹', '2025-09-01', '00:30:00', 0, NULL),
(2335, 1774, 'Working', 155, -2, 'Hi Caroline, We need to make the following fixes on the Salesforce side:  Message: Error: â€œData value too large.â€ This is caused by the 255-character limit. Could this field be changed to allow free-text input? At present, leads are failing to transfer to Salesforce when this limit is exceeded. Country Issue: Error: â€œThere\'s a problem with this country, even though it may appear correct. Please select a country/territory from the list of valid countries.â€ Could we obtain the full list of valid countries so we can check whether any countries are missing or incorrectly mapped? Next Expected Visit to London: Error: â€œBad value for restricted picklist field â€“ e.g. â€˜3 months +â€™.â€ Could the value â€œ3 months +â€ be added as an accepted option in Salesforce so that this field can be processed correctly?  @David, will be messaging you at 11:30 UK time for the 2FA.   Please let me know if you have any questions and confirm if youâ€™re able to understand the issues on the SF side.', '2025-09-01', '00:30:00', 0, NULL),
