(6659, 1784, 'Working', 287, -2, 'Impressions rose by 4.3% to 699.6K, showing improved reach over the period. However, clicks fell by 8.5% and CTR dropped significantly by 12.3% to 0.42%, suggesting that although the ads were being seen more, user engagement declined â€” likely due to creative fatigue.\n\nApp installs dropped by 31.3%, with the conversion rate down 24.8%, while cost per install rose sharply by 45.9% to Â£31.19, despite ad spend holding steady. This points to reduced efficiency with current creatives and highlights the need to test new creative angles. Once booking events are properly tracked, weâ€™ll also be able to explore alternative campaign objectives for better optimisation.\n\nGoogle campaigns remain paused. To assess performance accurately, itâ€™s essential to complete full tracking setup â€” including booking event tags and Firebase integration. Once thatâ€™s in place, we can begin optimising campaigns based on actual outcomes. We recommend prioritising this tracking implementation as soon as possible.', '2025-09-17', '01:30:00', 1, ''),
