(8592, 1774, 'Working', 294, 598, 'Hi Daniel,  When I embedded the form from HubSpot, it appeared like this:    However, the functionality we have is somewhat like this, as shown below.    Furthermore, this is passed to another form as shown below, combined together.    @Daniel,  So, what you mentioned is correct â€” we can use this embed. However, to meet the field requirements in our design, we would need this to be a custom form connected to Salesforce. We would also require some custom fields to be pre-created in the Salesforce Lead or Contact object, so that the userâ€™s collected form information can be passed once the connection to Salesforce has been established.\n\nHi Daniel,\n\nThe idea would be to capture these field values in a hidden field.\n\nî§\n\nAnd then pass them as hidden fields into this popup, I believe.\n\nî§\n\nWe are in discussions with the client regarding the Salesforce integration, so I have not started on it yet. They shared HubSpot code and mentioned that their HubSpot is connected to Salesforce. We are trying to clarify this, and I will update you once we know which direction the client would like to take. I will also let you know when I am ready to get started.', '2025-09-23', '00:30:00', 0, NULL),
