(14218, 1774, 'Working', 294, 598, 'Hi Hannah,  What you mentioned is correct â€” we just need a field in Helix to accommodate Service of Interest, which we can then leverage for the corresponding Hubs, Account Branches, and Marketing Channels for Contact Us. ----------------  Iâ€™ve added a form to https://previews.luux-media.com/apis/marketo-blackcloak.html. I tried submitting the form; however, it didnâ€™t work, and I received the following error: \"forms2.min.js:7 POST https://info.blackcloak.io/index.php/leadCapture/save2 400 (Bad Request)\" possibly due to captcha issue Yes, we can style the form accordingly. We can also add a script to populate hidden fields from UTM parameters. Weâ€™ll let you finalise the domain; however, could you temporarily whitelist previews.luux-media.com so we can test reCAPTCHA? Since we donâ€™t have control over the form submission, we may not be able to handle it directly â€” though this could possibly be managed from the Marketo end. ----------------  Create a new Lead in Greenwich   ----------------  Set new image on CLP LP for Constance\n', '2025-10-16', '01:00:00', 0, NULL),
(14219, 1774, 'Working', 294, 599, 'Hi Bhargavi, Iâ€™ve just tested this â€” I was able to obtain the Access Token; however, when I tried to create a Lead at (https://jetaviation--dev.sandbox.my.salesforce.com/services/data/v61.0/sobjects/Lead), I received the following error: [{\"errorCode\":\"NOT_FOUND\",\"message\":\"The requested resource does not exist\"}] I tried sending the following payload to create a lead: $leadData = [     \"FirstName\" => \"John02\",     \"LastName\" => \"Doe02\",     \"Company\" => \"Luux Media\",     \"Email\" => \"john.doe@luux-media.com\",     \"Phone\" => \"+447500656125\",     //\"LeadSource\" => \"Website\", ];  Regards Syed', '2025-10-16', '00:30:00', 0, NULL),
