(20695, 1774, 'Working', 294, 598, 'Hi Sanjeev,  Iâ€™ve just changed the AJAX submission URL from  https://bang-olufsen.luux-media.com/mail/callback.php  To   https://uat.bang-olufsen.com/en/gb/enquiry/mail/callback.php  Would you mind trying again and letting me know if youâ€™re able to submit the form now?  For video we have a third party link as below which should not be a problem once on production \nCould you also ensure that the outgoing connection to https://hooks.zapier.com/ is open? Thatâ€™s where we send the form submission in order to pass it back to our Google Sheet as well.  Regards Syed\n\nHi Sanjeev,  Iâ€™ve allowed CORS for uat.bang-olufsen.com and www.bang-olufsen.com, and Iâ€™ve also reverted the AJAX URL. Would you mind checking it again?  If it doesnâ€™t work, Iâ€™ll set up another test proxy on my end and try again, then get back to you.  Regards Syed', '2025-11-17', '00:30:00', 0, NULL),
(20696, 1774, 'Working', 294, 598, 'Hi Aria,\n\nHere are some additional details that should clarify everything.\n\n- No form is connected to the CRM yet.\n- Both forms(Madrid & Dubai) are currently connected to the Google Sheet.\n- Once the CRM is connected (it is not connected at the moment), all forms under one Meta account will be linked, and we cannot exclude a specific form from being sent to the CRM, as Estelle is expecting.\n- I need to check whether we can isolate the leads per form; if not, they will all be recorded in the same sheet and the same tab per account. For example, Madrid would record to the same sheet regardless of which form is used.\n- By Microsoft Forms, the client means Microsoft Excel Sheets. This would involve disconnecting the previous sheet and then reconnecting the Microsoft sheet. You may need to transfer all leads back to the Microsoft sheet.\n\nLet me know how youâ€™d like to proceed.\n\nRegards\nSyed\n\n\nHi Aria,  Since integrating with Microsoft Sheets will require a couple of Zapier connections, could you ask the client to share the shared folder with my email so that I can add the sheet there and then connect it accordingly? For the time being, Iâ€™ve connected the Google Sheet on two different tabs within this sheet. Regards Syed', '2025-11-17', '01:00:00', 0, NULL),
