(20718, 1774, 'Working', 294, 598, 'Hi Constance, We have now implemented the correct hreflang tags on the Madrid website (screenshot below). These tags signal to Google and other search engines which language version of the page should be shown to users based on their location and language preferences. Specifically: Spanish-speaking users will be directed to the Spanish version: https://longevity-hub.cliniquelaprairie.com/madrid/es/ English-speaking users will be directed to the English version: https://longevity-hub.cliniquelaprairie.com/madrid/ An x-default tag has also been added, which tells Google which version to serve when it cannot determine a userâ€™s language. In this case, the default falls back to the English version. These changes ensure that search engines correctly index and display the appropriate language version, helping to improve both user experience and search visibility in each region. The update is already in place and will be reflected by Google as it re-crawls the site. There is no default plugin feature available for this. It has been implemented at the code level specifically for Blog ID 5, which corresponds to the Madrid site within the network environment.', '2025-11-18', '01:00:00', 0, NULL),
