(20980, 1774, 'Working', 294, 599, 'Setup Sheet https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xg_WFSI7VAaFNbho1NNEPFDfKKlwcp3jaC0ZSm1nFkU/edit?gid=0#gid=0 for Internal Tracking so we can check what values are passed to salesforce', '2025-11-19', '02:00:00', 0, NULL),
(20981, 1774, 'Working', 294, 598, 'Hi Constance,\n\nCould you let me know where we should redirect these pages?\n\nhttps://longevity-hub.cliniquelaprairie.com/cellular-skincare/\nhttps://longevity-hub.cliniquelaprairie.com/doha/longevity-supplements/\nhttps://longevity-hub.cliniquelaprairie.com/dubai/cellular-skincare/\nhttps://longevity-hub.cliniquelaprairie.com/cellular-skincare/\nhttps://longevity-hub.cliniquelaprairie.com/es/programa-de-afiliacion/\n\n\nI donâ€™t see any inline CSS, so we can ignore that point.\nCould you share the pixel code so that we can add it to GTM?\nWeâ€™ve optimised the site using the WP Rocket plugin in terms of page speed as much as is feasible.\n\nThe LCP is 2.1 seconds on desktop, but it suddenly becomes 11.1 seconds on mobile. This can be safely ignored, as Google PageSpeed adjusts to different screen sizes when generating insights.\n\nWhy Mobile LCP Is Much Slower Than Desktop (Even on the Same Page)\n\nGoogle does not test mobile and desktop using the same performance profile.\n\n1. Google uses a very slow mobile device for testing\n\nFor mobile tests, PageSpeed uses:\nA mid-range Android phone\nWith CPU throttled to 4Ã— slower\nNetwork throttled to Slow 4G\nSimulated latency and packet loss\nThis means an LCP that takes 2 seconds on a laptop can easily take 10 seconds on simulated mobile.\nThis is perfectly normal.\n\n2. Mobile CPUs struggle with heavy JavaScript\n\nScripts that execute fast on desktop (GTM, UIkit, WP plugins, animations, sliders) take 5â€“10Ã— longer on Googleâ€™s simulated phone.\nSo render-blocking JS delays the hero element â†’ LCP increases heavily.\n\n3. Mobile networks load CSS & images much slower\n\nThe LCP image + UIkit + Slick CSS together create a large render-blocking chain.\n\nOn desktop: loads quickly\nOn mobile: waits longer â†’ LCP jumps\n\n4. Fonts and layout shifts affect mobile more\n\nRegards\nSyed', '2025-11-19', '01:00:00', 0, NULL),
