(21894, 1774, 'Working', 294, 598, 'Hi Matt,\n\nThe landing page we are building will be hosted at inquiry.thebeachclub.com, based on our current understanding, unless this has already been discussed previously and I may have missed it.\nThis will simply require you to point the A record for inquiry.thebeachclub.com to 67.227.191.110 in the domain registrar (Squarespace). This setup will be entirely separate from your current configuration on https://thebeachclub.com/home.\nIn this setup, we will host the files for you, and inquiry.thebeachclub.com will serve files from our server, routed via the A record you create as described above.\n\nCookie Popup:\nThe standard approach for implementing Cookie Consent Popups on HTML landing pages is to sign up with a third-party provider such as CookieYes, Cookiebot, OneTrust, Consent Manager, etc. These platforms allow you to build and customise the popup, after which they provide embed code or script snippets. You can then share those snippets with us, and we will place them on the landing page so that the popup appears when users visit the site.\nTerms and Conditions:\nWe already have the Privacy Policy link: https://thebeachclub.com/privacy-policy.\nCould you also create a Terms and Conditions page and share the link with us, so we can add it to the footer of the new landing page?\nî§¤\n\nStaging Site:\n\nThe Account Manager should be sharing the staging site link for the landing page with you, unless you have not received it yet.\n\nRegards\nSyed', '2025-11-21', '00:30:00', 0, NULL),
(21895, 1774, 'Working', 294, 599, 'Hi Lucy,\n\nIt appears that your leads are not consolidated and that leads created before the lead source field was added are not being displayed. As a result, any leads without a lead source are missing from your list.\nPlease find the attached sheet, where the leads within your Braze system have been manually mapped after checking each individual lead one by one. Each lead has been verified to ensure it exists in Braze and has been matched using the reference ID that was sent to Braze, based on the Zapier logs.\n\nThe leads from LUUX_AmanEssentials_SIGNUP_FORM_NOV_2025_Option1 are listed at the top, and the leads from LUUX_AmanEssentials_SIGNUP_FORM_NOV_2025_Option2 are listed at the bottom. Column E contains the reference ID for each individual lead.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions.\n\nRegards\nSyed', '2025-11-24', '02:00:00', 0, NULL),
(21896, 1774, 'Working', 294, 599, 'Hi Lucy,\n\nIt appears that your leads are not consolidated and that leads created before the lead source field was added are not being displayed. As a result, any leads without a lead source are missing from your list.\nPlease find the attached sheet, where the leads within your Braze system have been manually mapped after checking each individual lead one by one. Each lead has been verified to ensure it exists in Braze and has been matched using the reference ID that was sent to Braze, based on the Zapier logs.\n\nThe leads from LUUX_AmanEssentials_SIGNUP_FORM_NOV_2025_Option1 are listed at the top, and the leads from LUUX_AmanEssentials_SIGNUP_FORM_NOV_2025_Option2 are listed at the bottom. Column E contains the reference ID for each individual lead.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions.\n\nRegards\nSyed', '2025-11-24', '01:00:00', 0, NULL),
