(23539, 1774, 'Working', 294, 598, 'Hi Quentin,\n\nComing back to the jump issue we discussed â€” when I try to do it, I receive this error. Attached is the JSON for the flow.\n\n{\n  \"cause\": \"variable not found\",\n  \"description\": \"The value must be a valid \\\"string\\\"\",\n  \"error\": \"Flow.Step.Conditional.InvalidString\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"branchIndex\": 0,\n    \"variable\": \"{{steps.waitForConversationEvent_TGJX.event.message.body.text.text}}\"\n  }\n\n\n\nHere is the exact log:  â€” I am not sure whether you also need access to it.\nI have captured both events from the first message and the second message within the condition, yet it still throws an error. I may be doing something wrong?\n\n\n------------------------------------------\n\nHi @Quentin Hausser,  To put it simply, here is what we are aiming to achieve: On the form, there are three locations â€” Mayfair, Harrods, and Selfridges. Currently, the WhatsApp flow Number/Channel that is initiated to open a conversation with the user is always the same. However, the client expects three different numbers (WhatsApp channels) to be used depending on the selected location.          We can route this based on the location received from the form in the webhook; we just need to identify three active WhatsApp channels on three different numbers. Another question I have is: when a userâ€™s reply times out after wait of 48 hours, we need to re-initiate the conversation but after 48 hours,so we drop them into the timeout branch to rebuild the flow. Since we cannot copy the main branch steps(13 in number) directly into the timeout branch, is there a way to replicate those steps without manually recreating all the complex logic and routes again? Also, are we able to create three different agents and assign these agents to a userâ€™s conversation based on the location they selected on the form? The location is received in the webhook and is also stored in the contact record upon creation.  @Hannah Brand,  Could you also let me know what the email automation or location-based version would look like? Would it be similar to the example below, or do you have a specific template? Hi Team, A user has expressed interest in your service. Their email address is xyz@pqr.com and their contact number is +44 7500 656125.\n\n\n-----------------------------\n\nTraining Call B & O with their Developer', '2025-12-02', '02:00:00', 0, NULL),
